From ba7985bc3afa327504994960e65085445e07369b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:35:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] uhf: correct the rockchip.uhf.aidl-java module name to
 rockchip.uhf.aidl-V1-java

Real build failure, found by actually running the build (not by
inspection) - the previous commit's dependency name was wrong:

  echo "module services.core.unboosted missing dependencies:
  rockchip.uhf.aidl-java" && false

Traced through system/tools/aidl/build/aidl_interface_backends.go:
addJavaLibrary() names the generated module
i.versionedName(version) + "-java", and versionedName("") returns the
bare interface name only when version is the empty string. But
aidlInterface.nextVersion() (aidl_interface.go:793) returns "" only when
the interface is `unstable: true`; for anything else - including a
`stability: "vintf"` interface with zero frozen versions, which is what
rockchip.uhf.aidl is - it calls the package-level nextVersion([]string{})
helper, which returns "1" for an empty version list. So even before this
interface is ever frozen, its in-development "current" state is built as
version "1" in every generated module name: rockchip.uhf.aidl-V1-java,
not rockchip.uhf.aidl-java.

This is consistent with (and now actually explains) the VINTF manifest
fragments' pre-existing <version>1</version>, which earlier commits in
this series noted as "conventionally treated as version 1" without
tracing exactly why - this is why: it isn't a convention, it's what the
unversioned build literally is named as soon as stability: "vintf" is
set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 services/core/Android.bp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/Android.bp b/services/core/Android.bp
index c5cfe921..950ba17f 100644
--- a/services/core/Android.bp
+++ b/services/core/Android.bp
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@ java_library_static {
         "com.android.sysprop.watchdog",
         "ImmutabilityAnnotation",
         "securebox",
-        "rockchip.uhf.aidl-java", // AIDL, UHF-SRS-001 - see com.android.server.uhf.UhfHalTransport
+        "rockchip.uhf.aidl-V1-java", // AIDL, UHF-SRS-001 - see com.android.server.uhf.UhfHalTransport
     ],
     javac_shard_size: 50,
     javacflags: [
